\ draft-commit.8th -- Thinking 8th, Chapter 8
\ Verified with: 8th code/ch08/draft-commit.8th
\
\ G:clone makes a genuinely independent copy of a container, so a
\ draft can be freely edited without touching the committed value --
\ and committing is just cloning the draft back over it.

{ "top" : 0 , "bottom" : 0 , "left" : 0 , "right" : 0 } var, box
box @ G:clone var, draft drop

: begin-resize   \ --
  box @ G:clone draft ! ;

: commit-resize  \ --
  draft @ G:clone box ! ;

box @ "top" 10 m:! drop
box @ "bottom" 50 m:! drop

begin-resize
draft @ "top" 999 m:! drop

box @ "top" m:@ . cr drop      \ => 10
draft @ "top" m:@ . cr drop    \ => 999

commit-resize
box @ "top" m:@ . cr drop      \ => 999

bye
